Windows driver helper source and build material

libwdi is licensed under LGPL version 3 or later. Its complete source
and original copyright notices are in the accompanying source archive.
The supplied patch makes embedded resource timestamps honor
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH. The build recipe applies it to a fresh source tree.
Microsoft redistributable components retain the accompanying license.

On Linux, install GCC and 7-Zip. Download the pinned llvm_mingw and wdf
inputs in downloads.json and verify their SHA-256 digests. Extract the
toolchain and libwdi archives, then run:

python3 build.py --toolchain <llvm-mingw-directory> \
  --source <libwdi-directory> --wdf <wdfcoinstaller.msi> \
  --source-date-epoch $SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH --output <wdi-simple.exe>

The build runs only the native resource embedder. It does not execute
Windows programs or install a driver on the build host.
